  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-godot-preview",
      "text": "An independently installable Godot 4 preview plugin for DeepSeek Harness Desktop. It adds a **Godot Preview** view to the existing conversation details area without modifying Harness core."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "- Uses the active Harness session workspace as the Godot project root.\n- Validates `project.godot` and an existing Godot 4 executable.\n- Runs a Web Debug export and embeds the loopback preview in Harness.\n- Can launch and stop the native Godot project instead.\n- Watches project files with configurable debounce and single-flight rebuilds.\n- Coalesces changes during a build into at most one queued rebuild.\n- Preserves the last successful Web preview when a later export fails.\n- Shows bounded Host/export/runtime logs and structured failure locations.\n- Persists user-editable Godot path and preview preferences under `DSH_HOME`.\n- Stops managed exports, native runtimes, watchers, and preview servers on stop or plugin disposal."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "The package **never downloads or installs Godot** and does not bundle Chromium, Android/Xcode tooling, export templates, or mini-game SDKs."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- DeepSeek Harness Desktop with Web profile plugin support.\n- A user-installed Godot 4.x executable for real preview use.\n- A `project.godot` file at the active Harness session workspace root.\n- A Godot Web export preset named `Web` for Web preview.\n\nGDScript and the Compatibility renderer are recommended for portable Web previews."
    },
    {
      "section": "DSH community marketplace",
      "text": "Open **Settings → DSH Plugin Marketplace**, search for `dsh-godot-preview`, and choose **Install**. The community index discovers public GitHub repositories carrying the `dsh-plugin` topic."
    },
    {
      "section": "GitHub",
      "text": "```powershell\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:baiyuscc13724-max/dsh-godot-preview\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Release tarball",
      "text": "Download `dsh-godot-preview-0.1.0.tgz` from the matching GitHub Release, then run:\n\n```powershell\ndsh plugin --profile web add \"C:\\Downloads\\dsh-godot-preview-0.1.0.tgz\"\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "npm, if a registry release is published later",
      "text": "```powershell\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-godot-preview\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development checkout",
      "text": "```powershell\nnpm install\nnpm run check\ndsh plugin --profile web add \"C:\\path\\to\\dsh-godot-preview\"\n```\n\nRefresh the existing Harness Web page after installation if the prebuilt Client module was not reloaded automatically."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "1. Open a Harness session at a Godot project root.\n2. Open the **Godot Preview** conversation view.\n3. In **Settings → Godot Preview**, enter the absolute path to an existing Godot 4 executable. An empty path enables PATH discovery.\n4. Select **Web** or **Native**.\n5. Click **Start**.\n\nWeb mode serves only the most recent successful export. Native mode starts a managed Godot window. **Stop** is idempotent in both modes."
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "```text\nconversation.view Client\n  └─ GET/POST /api/godot-preview\n       └─ Host service router\n            ├─ project + executable validation\n\nThe prebuilt Client is a DSH module-loader factory (`window.__ModuleLoader__.load`), not a plain browser ESM entry. The Host registers its API through the public `webServer` service and disposes every resource through the plugin lifecycle."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development and verification",
      "text": "```powershell\nnpm run typecheck\nnpm test\nnpm run build\nnpm run pack:check\n\n`npm test` runs both:\n\n- Vitest integration suites against the real `createGodotPreviewService` implementation.\n- Node tests for the public HTTP adapter, settings persistence, and release-built Host modules."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development and verification",
      "text": "All automated Godot behavior is driven by `fixtures/fake-godot/fake-godot.cjs` through `process.execPath` plus a controlled argv prefix. It covers successful exports, script errors, timeouts, noisy logs, native runtimes, child-process trees, Chinese/space paths, rebuild coalescing, failure fallback, traversal defenses, and cleanup without downloading Godot.\n\nRun the end-to-end smoke demo:\n\n```powershell\nnpm run build:host\nnode demo/smoke.cjs\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Security summary",
